  <section class="info wrap">
    <h1>About <span class="accent">dshbase</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">dshbase is an independent, community-maintained guide and plugin directory for DeepSeek Harness (DSH).</p>

    <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
    <p>dshbase is operated by <strong>youliqn</strong>, an independent developer who has been running DeepSeek Harness since its launch in August 2026. You can find the operator on GitHub at <a href="https://github.com/ylwl1997" rel="noopener">github.com/ylwl1997</a>. This site is written and maintained by a human — every guide, test report, and plugin entry is based on actually installing and running the software, not scraped or auto-generated.</p>

    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>DeepSeek Harness launched with almost no English documentation, and its "everything is a plugin" model is genuinely new. We built dshbase to fill that gap: accurate install instructions, a tested plugin directory, and honest comparisons — the resource we wished existed when we started.</p>

    <h2>Our relationship to DeepSeek</h2>
    <p><strong>dshbase is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by DeepSeek or its parent company.</strong> It is an independent community project. We do not speak for DeepSeek, and errors here are ours, not theirs. The official repository is <a href="https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness" rel="noopener">github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness</a>.</p>

    <h2>How we test plugins</h2>
    <p>Each plugin entry in our directory is tagged with a test status. "Verified" means we installed it in a clean profile and it booted; "Unverified" means it is listed from its repository but we have not yet confirmed it runs. Star counts are pulled from GitHub and shown as a popularity signal, not an endorsement.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, corrections, or plugin submissions: <a href="mailto:hello@dshbase.com">hello@dshbase.com</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
